<title>JAPAN: Getz Bros to buy back Y10 bln worth of its shares.</title>
<headline>Getz Bros to buy back Y10 bln worth of its shares.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-10-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Getz Bros Co Ltd, an importer of medical supplies and equipment, said on Tuesday that the firm would buy back 10 billion yen worth, or six million, of its own shares.</p>
<p>The purchase price per share will be 1,570 yen, it said.</p>
<p>The aim of the buy-back is to return profits to shareholders, and the repurchase will be conducted between October 2 and October 22, the company also said.</p>
<p>Shares of Getz Bros stood at 1,500 yen in late Tuesday afternoon trade.</p>
</text>
